WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.260
Developing neurons compete for a limited supply of survival factor from their

2
00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.380
targets. That is the neurotrophic hypothesis.

3
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:13.560
Neurons are made in excess.

4
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.980
The target is the tissue an axon grows to and connects with.

5
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:19.920
It supplies the factor.

6
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.200
Neurons that get too little die by apoptosis.

7
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:28.240
Competition lets the target's supply decide how many neurons stay alive.

8
00:00:29.283 --> 00:00:31.523
Remove a target, and more neurons die.

9
00:00:32.523 --> 00:00:33.743
Add target, and fewer die.

10
00:00:34.603 --> 00:00:39.543
In chick spinal ganglia, many neurons formed and grew fibres before dying cells

11
00:00:39.543 --> 00:00:40.543
became conspicuous.

12
00:00:41.523 --> 00:00:43.163
The neurons were made, then lost.

13
00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:47.407
Nerve growth factor, or NGF, is the test case.

14
00:00:48.247 --> 00:00:52.147
Give young mammals extra NGF, and sympathetic ganglia enlarge.

15
00:00:53.187 --> 00:00:57.087
Block it with antiserum in newborn mice, and the ganglia waste away.

16
00:00:57.907 --> 00:01:00.567
But antibodies might bind something other than NGF.

17
00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:03.170
Genetics tests that doubt.

18
00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:10.210
Mice lacking NGF or its receptor, TrkA, lose sympathetic neurons and many sensory

19
00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:16.690
neurons. Without TrkA, the sympathetic ganglion still forms and axons start growing.

20
00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:18.670
Later the neurons die.

21
00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:20.510
What failed was survival.

22
00:01:21.583 --> 00:01:27.523
Add excess NGF during the death period in chick embryos, and more neurons escape the

23
00:01:27.523 --> 00:01:32.603
normal death. Count neurons and dying cells, and mark dividing cells to check.

24
00:01:33.423 --> 00:01:35.863
Early NGF can also increase division.

25
00:01:36.917 --> 00:01:39.357
How does a target support a distant cell body?

26
00:01:40.137 --> 00:01:41.937
The factor acts at the axon ending.

27
00:01:42.837 --> 00:01:47.017
A signal returns along the axon to the cell body to support survival.

28
00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.790
Dependence varies with population and age.

29
00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:54.510
Antiserum has much less effect in older animals.

30
00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:58.010
Limb motor neurons do not depend on NGF.

31
00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:03.570
Large sensory neurons that sense muscle stretch depend on a different neurotrophin.

32
00:02:04.483 --> 00:02:06.663
Survival is only part of the story.

33
00:02:07.663 --> 00:02:10.363
NGF also promotes axon growth and branching.

34
00:02:11.263 --> 00:02:16.423
When sympathetic neurons make their own NGF, axons still reach their tissues but

35
00:02:16.423 --> 00:02:18.063
branch sparsely inside them.

36
00:02:18.803 --> 00:02:21.523
Keeping neurons alive does not explain their wiring.

37
00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:28.067
A smaller closing point: for a fixed population, survival alone cannot save more

38
00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:29.147
neurons than were made.

39
00:02:30.007 --> 00:02:33.007
Extra factor can spare neurons that would otherwise die.
